WEBVTT

00:00:02.980 --> 00:00:05.400
The AV-98,
aka the Ingram patrol labor.

00:00:05.560 --> 00:00:08.520
6.02 tons.
8.02 meters high.

00:00:08.900 --> 00:00:12.700
SCB powered.
SCLM drive system.

00:00:12.990 --> 00:00:15.990
Armed and ready for combat with a
37 millimeter revolver and stun baton.

00:00:15.990 --> 00:00:19.540
Designed specifically
for police use...

00:00:19.990 --> 00:00:22.200
to make a psychological impact
on the community...

00:00:22.250 --> 00:00:25.540
to deter criminals
while making the public feel safe.

00:00:48.520 --> 00:00:51.280
yume wo sutenaide
You must not let go of your dreams

00:00:51.530 --> 00:00:54.070
me wo sorasanaide
And never turn your gaze away

00:00:55.070 --> 00:00:59.080
futari no ai mo kumoru yo
Yet even still love may cloud up and fade away

00:01:00.580 --> 00:01:03.450
utsumuita kata wo
And even though you comforted your love

00:01:03.580 --> 00:01:06.290
dakishimeta keredo
When he was feeling down

00:01:07.040 --> 00:01:11.300
samishisa mune ni tsumotta
Sadness was still weighing down his heavy heart

00:01:12.840 --> 00:01:18.510
yume wa kimi no buki no hazu da yo
Hang on tight to your dreams - they're weapons in your arsenal

00:01:18.720 --> 00:01:25.270
nee da kara kanashimi mo kinukete itte
You'll find that you can get through anything at all

00:01:25.770 --> 00:01:31.440
so never cry itsu mo kimi wo mitsumete 'ru yo
So never cry - you know I will always be watching over you

00:01:32.400 --> 00:01:37.280
fair na ikikata no kimi ga suki
What I love about you is your strong sense of fairness

00:01:37.910 --> 00:01:43.790
so never cry itsu mo kimi no soba ni iru yo
So never cry - you know I will always be right there by your side

00:01:44.410 --> 00:01:49.460
da kara mata asu e kakedashite
And so now you can face your future fearlessly

00:01:56.920 --> 00:02:00.930
I’m Takeo Kumagami

00:02:04.520 --> 00:02:07.180
Why don't we get some flowers
in here to cheer the place up?

00:02:07.180 --> 00:02:08.520
Soon as I'm done.

00:02:08.520 --> 00:02:12.020
There's nothing outside around here
except grass and weeds.

00:02:15.320 --> 00:02:17.150
These windows are filthy!

00:02:17.150 --> 00:02:18.950
You noticed it, you clean it.

00:02:20.700 --> 00:02:23.620
We should've finished all
this cleaning yesterday.

00:02:25.040 --> 00:02:27.960
We shouldn't let these things slide.

00:02:27.960 --> 00:02:30.540
This place could use
more spit and polish.

00:02:30.540 --> 00:02:34.500
Hey, that's a dishcloth
for the teapot!

00:02:34.500 --> 00:02:36.920
- Details, details.
- Ota!

00:02:36.920 --> 00:02:38.670
I wonder what he's like?

00:02:38.670 --> 00:02:41.640
I hope he's good to the Ingrams.

00:02:41.640 --> 00:02:42.760
Yeah.

00:02:42.760 --> 00:02:46.140
Takeo Kumagami's his name.
He sounds tough.

00:02:46.560 --> 00:02:49.060
You can't tell that from his name!
He's probably some big lug.

00:02:50.640 --> 00:02:53.360
Maybe he's all brawn,
like a certain other person.

00:02:54.230 --> 00:02:57.780
Come on, I'm just joking, Ota!

00:02:57.780 --> 00:02:59.400
He's a bit late.

00:02:59.400 --> 00:03:00.570
I hope nothing's happened.

00:03:01.070 --> 00:03:02.820
Maybe he chickened out.

00:03:02.820 --> 00:03:04.330
No way.

00:03:05.580 --> 00:03:07.540
Hey, someone's
walking up the road.

00:03:07.950 --> 00:03:10.160
Walking? That's stupid.

00:03:10.160 --> 00:03:11.210
What's he look like?

00:03:11.620 --> 00:03:13.000
Think it's Kumagami?

00:03:16.090 --> 00:03:17.670
It's a woman!

00:03:17.960 --> 00:03:18.960
What're we looking at?

00:03:21.630 --> 00:03:23.550
Ah, she's finally here!

00:03:24.800 --> 00:03:25.600
What?

00:03:25.600 --> 00:03:30.060
Captain’s Office

00:03:26.970 --> 00:03:30.060
Sorry I'm late.
I couldn't find a taxi.

00:03:30.680 --> 00:03:33.100
Taxis hate us. They avoid
this place like the plague.

00:03:33.560 --> 00:03:36.400
I thought you changed
your mind in the last minute.

00:03:36.400 --> 00:03:37.440
You're pulling my leg.

00:03:37.440 --> 00:03:39.860
Your experience is almost
too good to be true.

00:03:39.860 --> 00:03:41.820
I wish you'd joined my team.

00:03:42.240 --> 00:03:45.990
On the other hand, you'll get
more experience with Goto.

00:03:45.990 --> 00:03:48.120
His team is always
getting into trouble.

00:03:48.580 --> 00:03:49.870
Beg your pardon?

00:03:49.870 --> 00:03:50.660
About work.

00:03:51.000 --> 00:03:55.500
How long will you need to get up
to speed with the Labor system?

00:03:55.500 --> 00:03:57.420
I'll need two days
for the basic theory.

00:03:57.840 --> 00:04:02.260
Mastering it shouldn't
take more than a week.

00:04:02.260 --> 00:04:03.260
Good!

00:04:03.260 --> 00:04:04.930
Hopefully your uniform
will be here by then.

00:04:05.390 --> 00:04:07.220
I'll introduce you to your team.

00:04:12.730 --> 00:04:16.440
Her assignment won't be
official for ten more days.

00:04:16.440 --> 00:04:19.690
But she'll start
training with you today.

00:04:19.690 --> 00:04:20.990
This is Takeo Kumagami.

00:04:22.900 --> 00:04:23.950
I'm Kumagami.

00:04:24.530 --> 00:04:27.990
Teach her everything
you know about Ingrams.

00:04:27.990 --> 00:04:29.580
Get to know each other.

00:04:30.950 --> 00:04:32.160
I'm pleased to meet you.

00:04:32.500 --> 00:04:34.210
Pleased to meet you.

00:04:37.000 --> 00:04:39.000
- She's pretty.
- Sort of.

00:04:39.000 --> 00:04:41.460
Bet she's sorry
she ever saw this dump.

00:04:41.460 --> 00:04:43.840
But she looks nice.

00:04:44.300 --> 00:04:46.260
I think she'll fit right in.

00:04:48.680 --> 00:04:49.890
Here you go.

00:04:50.220 --> 00:04:51.520
Thank you.

00:04:51.520 --> 00:04:54.770
You'll probably want to
bring in your own cup.

00:04:54.770 --> 00:04:56.520
That's what we've all done.

00:04:57.020 --> 00:04:58.860
Anything I can do around here?

00:04:59.270 --> 00:05:02.820
Nothing, we're fine. Just sit back
and make yourself at home.

00:05:03.280 --> 00:05:05.610
I'd like to dive in
as soon as possible.

00:05:08.700 --> 00:05:09.740
There's nothing to do.

00:05:10.120 --> 00:05:16.000
Uh, I guess you could enter
some data for me.

00:05:16.830 --> 00:05:17.460
Sure.

00:05:19.590 --> 00:05:21.840
Good. That's it.

00:05:21.840 --> 00:05:22.920
Think you've got it?

00:05:23.340 --> 00:05:27.050
Yes, it's just a bit different
from the program I used to use.

00:05:27.050 --> 00:05:29.600
Take your time,
I'm in no hurry.

00:05:42.270 --> 00:05:46.360
I can't stand people like her.
They have too much spunk.

00:05:46.360 --> 00:05:49.200
You can't judge a woman
on your first impression.

00:05:49.570 --> 00:05:52.660
I think you might
have a point there, Hiromi.

00:05:52.660 --> 00:05:53.910
Oh yeah?

00:05:53.910 --> 00:05:55.250
Officer Shinohara?

00:05:57.210 --> 00:06:01.000
Officer Izumi is looking for you.
She's in the computer room.

00:06:01.000 --> 00:06:02.420
Thanks.

00:06:06.170 --> 00:06:07.470
Sorry! I'll get those.

00:06:12.350 --> 00:06:13.390
Thank you.

00:06:13.390 --> 00:06:14.720
Sorry about that.

00:06:22.360 --> 00:06:24.900
She must've heard us
talking about her.

00:06:27.900 --> 00:06:29.450
Promotion exam, huh?

00:06:35.080 --> 00:06:36.540
Yo, Noa, where are you?

00:06:36.540 --> 00:06:38.120
Over here!

00:06:40.040 --> 00:06:43.840
Jeez, I've been looking
all over for you.

00:06:44.210 --> 00:06:45.380
Sorry.

00:06:45.380 --> 00:06:49.090
I had problems getting a hard copy,
but Shinshi helped me out.

00:06:49.380 --> 00:06:51.180
Dinner's almost done.

00:06:51.180 --> 00:06:52.850
I'll come help.

00:06:58.770 --> 00:07:00.230
You'll just get in my way.

00:07:00.230 --> 00:07:01.350
Creep!

00:07:06.150 --> 00:07:09.280
Hiromi, did you do all this?
Unreal!

00:07:10.450 --> 00:07:11.910
It's the dinner of my dreams!

00:07:11.910 --> 00:07:13.740
- Grace!
- Dibs on that!

00:07:14.120 --> 00:07:16.290
I didn't make all this.

00:07:16.290 --> 00:07:17.790
Then who did?

00:07:18.120 --> 00:07:19.290
Kumagami.

00:07:21.790 --> 00:07:22.920
Where'd she get to?

00:07:22.920 --> 00:07:23.960
She said
she had something to do.

00:07:25.250 --> 00:07:26.750
She could have
eaten with us at least.

00:07:28.630 --> 00:07:30.800
So what do you
think of Kumagami?

00:07:30.800 --> 00:07:31.760
What do you mean?

00:07:33.180 --> 00:07:35.930
I can't figure her out.

00:07:36.310 --> 00:07:37.890
What are you talking about?

00:07:37.890 --> 00:07:41.520
She's bubbly, a good cook.
What's the problem?

00:07:41.520 --> 00:07:42.390
Hands off! That's mine!

00:07:42.850 --> 00:07:46.730
<i>And</i> she's an incredible typist.

00:07:46.730 --> 00:07:48.480
Super fast.

00:07:49.400 --> 00:07:52.320
She doesn't fit in,
that's all I'm saying.

00:07:52.320 --> 00:07:53.910
She's our newest comrade.

00:07:53.910 --> 00:07:55.620
Stop slagging her!

00:07:55.950 --> 00:07:57.870
You're being too critical.

00:07:57.870 --> 00:08:00.910
We'll make her fit in soon enough.

00:08:00.910 --> 00:08:02.160
That's for sure!

00:08:16.010 --> 00:08:17.180
Morning, Shige.

00:08:17.970 --> 00:08:19.010
Morning.

00:08:19.010 --> 00:08:21.430
- Noa's sure psyched today.
- Huh?

00:08:22.180 --> 00:08:23.390
See?

00:08:24.940 --> 00:08:26.730
That's Kumagami.

00:08:27.230 --> 00:08:28.900
Incredible, isn't she?

00:08:29.360 --> 00:08:32.320
It's only taken her a day to master
the Labor's basic movement.

00:08:35.070 --> 00:08:37.070
Good morning, Officer Shinohara.

00:08:37.070 --> 00:08:38.620
Good morning.

00:08:38.620 --> 00:08:42.620
Mr. Shiba, would you check
the motion trace setting?

00:08:42.620 --> 00:08:44.790
- It feels slow today.
- Really?

00:08:45.460 --> 00:08:47.540
I guess I shouldn't have
fiddled with it last night.

00:08:49.840 --> 00:08:53.050
Have you used Labors before?

00:08:53.380 --> 00:08:54.090
No.

00:08:55.510 --> 00:08:57.050
You pick things up pretty fast.

00:08:57.720 --> 00:09:01.560
If you can remember the basics,
the rest is just technique.

00:09:01.560 --> 00:09:04.270
Labors, linguistics, computers,
they're all the same.

00:09:04.770 --> 00:09:06.940
Theories don't work
in real combat.

00:09:06.940 --> 00:09:09.110
All the better for me to get
valuable experience.

00:09:10.400 --> 00:09:13.070
Kumagami,
could you look at this?

00:09:13.070 --> 00:09:14.030
Certainly.

00:09:14.030 --> 00:09:19.120
I want to master the Ingram while
Division 2 is still on standby.

00:09:19.450 --> 00:09:20.240
You're sure earnest.

00:09:21.870 --> 00:09:23.450
And that's a surprise?

00:09:26.250 --> 00:09:28.670
He's right. I shouldn't judge
on first impressions.

00:09:32.550 --> 00:09:33.840
Hello, Shinohara.

00:09:33.840 --> 00:09:35.510
Good morning, sir.

00:09:35.510 --> 00:09:36.930
Is Kumagami around?

00:09:36.930 --> 00:09:38.890
- She's in back.
- In back, huh?

00:09:40.720 --> 00:09:41.810
Captain...

00:09:42.890 --> 00:09:45.390
Are you thinking of
making her a Forward?

00:09:46.180 --> 00:09:49.440
I'll have to wait and see
how she does.

00:09:49.440 --> 00:09:53.110
But there's no reason
we can't reorganize the positions.

00:09:56.450 --> 00:09:57.990
This can't be right.

00:09:58.490 --> 00:09:59.410
Morning.

00:10:00.240 --> 00:10:02.580
Asuma, can you
show me something here?

00:10:03.410 --> 00:10:06.330
My box won't run this command.

00:10:07.790 --> 00:10:08.920
Sure you entered it right?

00:10:09.420 --> 00:10:11.590
I've tried it a million times,
but it won't work.

00:10:12.880 --> 00:10:15.010
Oh, here.
You didn't put a space in.

00:10:15.340 --> 00:10:16.760
Huh? Where?

00:10:17.260 --> 00:10:19.720
Right here.
It won't work without a space.

00:10:22.180 --> 00:10:23.430
Oh, yeah?

00:10:24.260 --> 00:10:26.220
Man, go figure!

00:10:27.680 --> 00:10:29.190
Good morning.

00:10:29.560 --> 00:10:31.020
Good morning.

00:10:33.110 --> 00:10:34.400
Come here a minute.

00:10:38.070 --> 00:10:40.860
Hey, you can't keep counting on me
to bail you out all the time.

00:10:40.860 --> 00:10:42.570
What crawled up your butt?

00:10:42.950 --> 00:10:46.330
Watch yourself, or you'll
lose your position as Forward.

00:10:46.750 --> 00:10:48.040
Better pull your socks up.

00:10:48.460 --> 00:10:49.540
What do you mean?

00:10:49.540 --> 00:10:52.330
The captain said he might
reorganize our division.

00:10:53.880 --> 00:10:57.130
Kumagami's already
mastered the Ingram.

00:10:57.630 --> 00:10:59.050
She's awesome.

00:11:00.260 --> 00:11:01.970
Everyone's got their own talents.

00:11:02.260 --> 00:11:04.640
Just do your best,
that's all I'm saying.

00:11:08.480 --> 00:11:12.810
Another day, another dollar.
What a day.

00:11:27.290 --> 00:11:29.500
Aren't you going home?

00:11:29.870 --> 00:11:31.420
No, I'm gonna work out.

00:11:32.000 --> 00:11:34.840
Can I ask you something?

00:11:34.840 --> 00:11:35.460
Sure.

00:11:36.040 --> 00:11:38.210
You've got so much going for you.

00:11:38.210 --> 00:11:40.420
How come you were sent here,
of all places?

00:11:45.260 --> 00:11:48.680
Don't you have
any pride in your work?

00:11:50.730 --> 00:11:54.650
With an attitude like that,
you'll never improve or advance.

00:11:56.190 --> 00:11:58.980
I chose to come here.

00:11:58.980 --> 00:12:02.110
I'm always looking for
a chance to improve myself.

00:12:03.990 --> 00:12:04.610
Wait.

00:12:09.580 --> 00:12:10.500
Look outside.

00:12:12.000 --> 00:12:13.750
What's gotten into them?

00:12:16.630 --> 00:12:18.460
Now this is interesting.

00:12:19.670 --> 00:12:20.920
Oh, nothing.

00:12:39.900 --> 00:12:41.780
Oh, no, not again!

00:12:46.030 --> 00:12:49.030
I did it by the book,
with a space and everything!

00:12:51.330 --> 00:12:52.200
Asuma.

00:12:54.710 --> 00:12:55.540
Let me see.

00:12:58.920 --> 00:13:00.550
- Get it?
- Got it.

00:13:02.340 --> 00:13:05.340
I can't keep up with Kumagami!

00:13:05.340 --> 00:13:05.840
Why not?

00:13:06.510 --> 00:13:07.890
It's kinda obvious.

00:13:07.890 --> 00:13:13.560
She's a great cook, she's an athlete,
and she can pilot an Ingram.

00:13:14.520 --> 00:13:15.770
And then there's me.

00:13:17.440 --> 00:13:18.810
I'll show you something cool.

00:13:24.900 --> 00:13:26.570
These are simulations
of you and Ota.

00:13:28.990 --> 00:13:31.330
First: Damage
inflicted on opponents.

00:13:31.790 --> 00:13:34.200
Ota inflicts more damage,
so he's stronger.

00:13:36.330 --> 00:13:40.250
Next, reaction time to commands:
Ota is faster.

00:13:42.000 --> 00:13:44.800
So you're slower and
weaker than Ota.

00:13:46.170 --> 00:13:50.220
Now, the motion data
from both units.

00:13:52.970 --> 00:13:55.680
Ota's gestures are larger.

00:13:56.480 --> 00:13:59.560
You take longer to begin
following an order.

00:13:59.900 --> 00:14:01.570
But you finish
your response sooner.

00:14:02.020 --> 00:14:05.530
What I'm saying is,
you're a lot more efficient.

00:14:05.530 --> 00:14:06.570
Got it?

00:14:06.570 --> 00:14:07.950
Yeah, I think so.

00:14:08.860 --> 00:14:12.620
You can't judge someone
on any single factor.

00:14:13.290 --> 00:14:15.330
I dunno what Kumagami is like...

00:14:15.330 --> 00:14:18.670
but it's pointless to
judge her by appearance.

00:14:19.580 --> 00:14:20.500
I mean that.

00:14:21.960 --> 00:14:23.920
See ya tomorrow.
Don't catch a cold.

00:14:24.550 --> 00:14:25.590
Uh, good night.

00:14:30.720 --> 00:14:31.550
Chin up!

00:14:41.150 --> 00:14:42.020
Come in.

00:14:42.810 --> 00:14:43.570
You wanted to see me?

00:14:44.480 --> 00:14:45.940
Yeah, your uniform's arrived.

00:14:46.610 --> 00:14:48.900
And I've decided
on your position.

00:15:09.470 --> 00:15:11.470
Well? Think you're up to it?

00:15:11.470 --> 00:15:12.760
If this is what you want.

00:15:13.430 --> 00:15:15.470
Just give it a shot.

00:15:19.770 --> 00:15:21.140
Come in.

00:15:21.520 --> 00:15:23.360
Oh, you got your uniform!

00:15:24.270 --> 00:15:26.360
I'm glad it came in time
for my official appointment.

00:15:26.820 --> 00:15:28.110
Tomorrow's the big day, huh?

00:15:29.990 --> 00:15:32.320
About the other day...

00:15:36.790 --> 00:15:38.080
We'll talk later.

00:15:39.080 --> 00:15:41.500
Before we mobilize, I want to
adjust the positions slightly.

00:15:41.750 --> 00:15:43.210
What, now?

00:15:43.670 --> 00:15:48.050
As of today, Kumagami
will run command car 2.

00:15:48.380 --> 00:15:51.720
Officer Shinshi will handle carrier 2.

00:15:52.090 --> 00:15:52.630
Move out.

00:15:55.260 --> 00:15:57.600
What are you doing, Captain?

00:15:57.600 --> 00:15:59.810
How can you let this...

00:15:59.810 --> 00:16:01.060
I feel sorry for her!

00:16:01.060 --> 00:16:03.190
Why should she put up with him?
I'll take sacrifice!

00:16:04.060 --> 00:16:08.070
Save it for later.
Now, you have some work to do.

00:16:09.530 --> 00:16:11.150
What're you waiting for?

00:16:11.650 --> 00:16:14.530
You have the right to refuse
an unreasonable order.

00:16:14.530 --> 00:16:15.620
I could handle it for you.

00:16:18.990 --> 00:16:21.500
Thank you, but I'm fine.

00:16:21.500 --> 00:16:23.580
Do you know how to
operate the command car?

00:16:24.080 --> 00:16:25.130
Of course.

00:16:35.720 --> 00:16:39.060
I can't allow you to do this!
I realize it's a direct command...

00:16:39.060 --> 00:16:43.980
but this is a dangerous situation,
and it's my right and duty to protest!

00:16:46.940 --> 00:16:52.110
You can't let someone
like that give the orders!

00:16:52.860 --> 00:16:54.820
This doesn't look good.

00:16:54.820 --> 00:16:56.820
Thanks for coming out.

00:16:57.320 --> 00:16:59.830
Hello. Could you
give me an update?

00:17:00.870 --> 00:17:02.580
It's ugly, I tell ya.

00:17:02.580 --> 00:17:06.790
Two construction Labors are
acting out of control.

00:17:06.790 --> 00:17:09.880
They're hiding underground
in the sewers.

00:17:09.880 --> 00:17:12.510
And they've taken
one of our crew hostage.

00:17:13.970 --> 00:17:16.220
A hostage. That's bad.

00:17:18.140 --> 00:17:19.260
Captain!

00:17:19.260 --> 00:17:21.970
Questions later.
Get underground.

00:17:31.900 --> 00:17:35.570
We've just started
rebuilding the sewer.

00:17:35.860 --> 00:17:37.570
It's been temporarily widened.

00:17:38.200 --> 00:17:40.280
- Can we surround them?
- Here and here.

00:17:40.280 --> 00:17:41.990
But we need to
seal off this access tunnel.

00:17:41.990 --> 00:17:44.450
Otherwise, we'll need
lots of back up.

00:17:45.580 --> 00:17:47.170
Is this a support structure?

00:17:47.500 --> 00:17:51.000
It used to be,
but we aren't using it now.

00:17:51.000 --> 00:17:52.550
It's just a steel plate.

00:17:53.000 --> 00:17:56.170
- How tall?
- About ten meters, give or take.

00:17:57.550 --> 00:17:58.640
We could use that.

00:18:09.350 --> 00:18:11.440
Officer Ota, do you read me?

00:18:11.440 --> 00:18:12.980
We have a preliminary plan.

00:18:12.980 --> 00:18:14.610
I'm going to transmit a map.

00:18:14.610 --> 00:18:15.780
Roger. Go ahead.

00:18:23.240 --> 00:18:28.160
Lure them to coordinates K2,
where unit 1 will ambush them.

00:18:28.160 --> 00:18:28.960
Roger.

00:18:34.000 --> 00:18:35.000
Damn you!

00:18:43.220 --> 00:18:46.270
Ota, stand by
till you hear from us.

00:18:47.270 --> 00:18:50.100
They are probably
heading towards unit 1.

00:18:50.520 --> 00:18:53.310
I hope he's okay.
He did scream.

00:19:00.700 --> 00:19:02.950
This place is creepy.
It's so wet.

00:19:02.950 --> 00:19:04.950
Alphonse could rust.

00:19:04.950 --> 00:19:06.200
Noa, do you read me?

00:19:06.200 --> 00:19:07.000
Yeah?

00:19:07.410 --> 00:19:08.540
Change of plans.

00:19:08.540 --> 00:19:13.540
Chase the perps to
coordinates K2 and force them in.

00:19:13.840 --> 00:19:16.130
How am I supposed to
force them in?

00:19:16.130 --> 00:19:17.010
Figure it out.

00:19:22.720 --> 00:19:24.680
Noa, the legs are
the most vulnerable!

00:19:30.890 --> 00:19:31.810
Got ya!

00:19:52.040 --> 00:19:52.920
Halt!

00:19:52.920 --> 00:19:54.790
- Don't chase them!
- Why not?

00:19:55.340 --> 00:19:59.090
We'll get them from both sides
and catch them at the same time.

00:19:59.510 --> 00:20:02.630
Yeah, what she says!
Move to the exit and seal it off.

00:20:02.630 --> 00:20:04.260
Unit 2, continue pursuit.

00:20:06.100 --> 00:20:08.220
Keep out

00:20:13.730 --> 00:20:16.190
End of the line for you, pal!

00:20:26.820 --> 00:20:27.910
Permission to fire!

00:20:27.910 --> 00:20:29.790
No, they have a hostage.

00:20:29.790 --> 00:20:30.950
Come on!

00:20:30.950 --> 00:20:35.460
Officer Ota, your accuracy on
moving targets is only 40%.

00:20:44.300 --> 00:20:47.220
Release the hostage at once,
or I'll fire.

00:20:54.560 --> 00:20:56.690
Help! I don't wanna die!

00:20:56.690 --> 00:20:58.230
Look at this!

00:20:59.520 --> 00:21:02.030
- What're you gonna do?
- Save me!

00:21:02.030 --> 00:21:03.190
I'll shoot him!

00:21:03.530 --> 00:21:05.860
Is that what you want?

00:21:06.570 --> 00:21:07.740
You asked for it!

00:21:20.040 --> 00:21:21.550
She's good.

00:21:22.340 --> 00:21:23.300
Yup.

00:21:30.180 --> 00:21:31.970
Can I ask you something?

00:21:33.310 --> 00:21:35.520
How did you know
he didn't have a gun?

00:21:35.520 --> 00:21:37.650
Just a feeling.

00:21:38.310 --> 00:21:42.110
If he had a gun, he wouldn't
need to hide in the sewer.

00:21:43.610 --> 00:21:44.780
Good point.

00:21:46.280 --> 00:21:47.780
I never thought of that.

00:21:48.490 --> 00:21:51.120
I'm gonna learn a lot from you.

00:21:56.460 --> 00:21:57.290
Thanks.

00:21:58.540 --> 00:21:59.750
No probs.

00:22:03.000 --> 00:22:04.880
Lieutenant?

00:22:06.920 --> 00:22:09.260
After training with
the Hong Kong Police...

00:22:09.260 --> 00:22:11.050
Lt. Kumagami was assigned
to Foreign Affairs.

00:22:11.600 --> 00:22:15.020
InterPol wanted her, but
she decided to join our team.

00:22:15.020 --> 00:22:16.480
It was my decision.

00:22:17.270 --> 00:22:20.270
We mobilized before
I could formally introduce her.

00:22:20.690 --> 00:22:22.610
I think she proved herself
last night.

00:22:22.610 --> 00:22:23.860
A top gun.

00:22:24.190 --> 00:22:25.940
What a record!

00:22:26.280 --> 00:22:28.490
A lieutenant!

00:22:29.660 --> 00:22:31.280
I'll take your questions now.

00:22:31.280 --> 00:22:33.330
A lieutenant.

00:22:33.330 --> 00:22:34.950
Be good to her now.

00:22:35.790 --> 00:22:38.920
I'm looking forward
to working with you all.

00:22:42.420 --> 00:22:45.630
dakishimete MIDNIGHT BLUE
Just hold me tightly, Midnight Blue

00:22:45.760 --> 00:22:49.340
kon'ya reiji no basu ni nottara
If I can make it to the bus stop by midnight

00:22:51.680 --> 00:22:55.600
ichido-kiri nara dekiru hazu da kara
I know I can do it, if only just once

00:23:03.020 --> 00:23:05.110
yume ni hikizurare
Pulled into my dream I find that I wake up

00:23:05.230 --> 00:23:08.030
ore wa ase mamire no Lonely
Drenched in sweat and feeling lonely

00:23:08.110 --> 00:23:12.620
hanashi-aite no TV suitchi hipparu
I turn off the TV I've been listening to

00:23:15.280 --> 00:23:17.290
ashita ichinichi wa
Tomorrow I will spend the whole day

00:23:17.370 --> 00:23:20.120
akogareta machi no gomi no naka
In the city of my dreams, amidst the old dust

00:23:20.370 --> 00:23:24.290
hayaku mein sutoriito ni sawaritai no sa
I want to feel the main street beneath my feet soon

00:23:27.460 --> 00:23:30.800
manazashi dake wa itsu demo
I plan to always look on the brighter side

00:23:33.430 --> 00:23:36.060
ue wo muite 'ru tsumori
Keep my chin up, look to the future

00:23:36.010 --> 00:23:38.600
tatta hitotsu no michi da kara
After all, there's only one path I can travel

00:23:38.600 --> 00:23:41.810
dakishimete MIDNIGHT BLUE
Just hold me tightly, Midnight Blue

00:23:42.060 --> 00:23:45.900
kon'ya reiji no basu ni nottara
If I can make it to the bus stop by midnight

00:23:48.280 --> 00:23:52.070
ichido-kiri nara dekiru hazu da kara
I know I can do it, if only just once

00:23:54.240 --> 00:23:58.120
kon'ya reiji no basu ni nottara
If I can make it to the bus stop by midnight

00:24:00.460 --> 00:24:04.750
ichido-kiri nara dekiru hazu da kara
I know I can do it, if only just once

00:24:06.250 --> 00:24:09.420
This story is fiction...

00:24:06.250 --> 00:24:09.420
but in 10 years, who knows?

00:24:13.550 --> 00:24:15.390
I dunno what kind of
karmic mess this is!

00:24:15.390 --> 00:24:17.640
We're mobilized
in a condemned building...

00:24:17.640 --> 00:24:21.890
where we're attacked
from all sides.

00:24:21.890 --> 00:24:23.350
What've they got against us?

00:24:23.350 --> 00:24:25.810
What do they want
with our platoon?

00:24:25.810 --> 00:24:28.440
And why have they lured us into
this derelict building?

00:24:28.440 --> 00:24:32.030
We're being summoned.
Someone's calling us from the grave!

00:24:32.030 --> 00:24:33.820
Coming next,
"A Voice in the Darkness."

00:24:34.030 --> 00:24:35.820
Target: Locked on!

00:24:34.320 --> 00:24:39.870
Next episode

00:24:34.320 --> 00:24:39.870
A Voice in the Darkness
